course: dictionary
lesson: 3600
title: Fife, the flute and the place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and a capital letter tells you which one is meant. A fife is a small flute with a high sound. It has no keys, and it is played mainly in military marching bands, often with drums.
explain: Fife with a capital F is a place: a region in eastern Scotland, between the Firth of Forth and the Firth of Tay. «In Fife, Ruaridh, 9, hears the class trip is to a castle with a hundred steps.» The capital F shows that Fife is a place name, not an instrument.
explain: Check the clues around the word. Is the sentence talking about music, a marching band or a map? If it mentions a region, a town or a country, it is the place. If it mentions playing, sounds or marching, it is the instrument.
fact: A fife is a small, high-sounding flute without keys.
fact: Fife and drum bands marched with armies, such as in the American Revolution.
fact: Fife, with a capital letter, is a region in eastern Scotland, and St Andrews is in Fife.
fact: Proper nouns, such as place names, always start with a capital letter.
fact: «The Kingdom of Fife» and «fife and drum» are useful phrases to remember.
exercise: «In Fife, Ruaridh, 9, hears the class trip is to a castle with a hundred steps.» Where is Fife? | Wales | *In eastern Scotland | In the middle of the sea | In London
exercise: What is a fife? | A large drum with a deep sound | A type of boat | A big brass horn | *A small, high-sounding flute without keys
exercise: Fife and drum bands marched together. Which other instrument did they play? | Harp | Piano | *Drum
exercise: Why does «Fife» start with a capital letter when it means the region? | Because it is a musical instrument | Because it is a colour | *Because it is the name of a place | Because it starts a new paragraph
test: St Andrews is in which region of Scotland? | Cornwall | *Fife | Yorkshire
test: Which phrase is about a Scottish region? | a small flute | fife and drum | a fife | *the Kingdom of Fife
exam: Which phrase from the lesson names a Scottish region? | a fife | fife and drum | marching band | *the Kingdom of Fife
